IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nzs-types`
IMPORT `nzs-entitlement`
IMPORT `nzs-overseas`
IMPORT `nzs-fund`
IMPORT `nzs-goal`

-- New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from
-- ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2001_84.txt, not from the code.
-- The rates and the s 8(4) requirements are made up (both are lost in the
-- converted text).

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

-- Born 1 March 1960, requirement req, NZ years since 20, NZ and Pacific years
-- since 20, years since 50; resident; applied 1 January 2025.
GIVEN req IS A NUMBER, nz IS A NUMBER, pacific IS A NUMBER, fifty IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Applicant
`applicant needing` req `with` nz `and` pacific `and` fifty MEANS
    Applicant OF Date 1 3 1960, FALSE, TRUE, req, nz, pacific, fifty, FALSE, Date 1 1 1985, Date 1 1 2025, NOTHING

`a long resident` MEANS `applicant needing` 10 `with` 40 `and` 40 `and` 15

`the rates` MEANS `Rates in force` OF 1000, 920, 760, 300

GIVEN status IS A `Relationship status`, alone IS A BOOLEAN, care IS A BOOLEAN, weeks IS A NUMBER, funded IS A BOOLEAN, children IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Rate facts`
`rate facts` status alone care weeks funded children MEANS
    `Rate facts` OF status, (Household OF TRUE, NOT alone), care, weeks, funded, children

`couple` MEANS `married, in a civil union, or in a de facto relationship`

GIVEN week IS A NUMBER, total IS A NUMBER, unforeseeable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Absence facts`
`absent week` week `of` total `, unforeseeable:` unforeseeable MEANS
    `Absence facts` OF week, total, unforeseeable, 0, 0, 0

GIVEN mo IS A NUMBER, dy IS A NUMBER, yr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Absence facts`
`residence of` mo `months` dy `days, years` yr MEANS
    `Absence facts` OF 0, 0, FALSE, mo, dy, yr

§§ `Goal 1 — entitlement`

#ASSERT `the age of someone born` (Date 1 3 1960) `on` (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS 64
#ASSERT `the age of someone born` (Date 1 3 1960) `on` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS 65

-- s 8A: arrived at 50 (1 January 2025, born 1 January 1975): 15 calendar years to the 65th birthday (F1, changed after the independent pass)
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 1 1 1975, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, Date 1 1 2025, Date 1 1 2040, NOTHING) EQUALS 15
-- arrived 1 July 2025 at 50: 14 years and 184 days
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 1 1 1975, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 1 1 2040, NOTHING) EQUALS 14 PLUS (184 DIVIDED BY 365.25)
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 1 1 1970, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, Date 1 1 2025, Date 1 1 2040, NOTHING) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 2 1 1980, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, Date 1 1 2025, Date 1 1 2045, NOTHING) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 1 1 1975, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, Date 1 1 2025, Date 1 1 2040, NOTHING) EQUALS 20
-- s 8A(3)(b): the table is lower than the days to 65
#ASSERT `the total time requirement in years for` (Applicant OF Date 1 1 1975, FALSE, TRUE, 12, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, Date 1 1 2025, Date 1 1 2040, NOTHING) EQUALS 12

-- s 8
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 10 `with` 10 `and` 10 `and` 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 10 `with` 9 `and` 10 `and` 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 10 `with` 10 `and` 10 `and` 4) EQUALS FALSE
-- the s 8 example: 14 years needed; 12 in New Zealand, 1 in the Cook Islands, 1 in Niue
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 14 `with` 12 `and` 14 `and` 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 14 `with` 12 `and` 13 `and` 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (`applicant needing` 14 `with` 9 `and` 14 `and` 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `meets the residential qualification` (Applicant OF Date 1 3 1960, FALSE, FALSE, 10, 40, 40, 15, FALSE, Date 1 1 1985, Date 1 1 2025, NOTHING) EQUALS FALSE

-- s 7
#ASSERT `is entitled to New Zealand superannuation` `a long resident` `on` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is entitled to New Zealand superannuation` `a long resident` `on` (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is entitled to New Zealand superannuation` (Applicant OF Date 1 3 1960, TRUE, TRUE, 10, 40, 40, 15, FALSE, Date 1 1 1985, Date 1 1 2025, NOTHING) `on` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 11
#ASSERT `the day New Zealand superannuation commences for` `a long resident` EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day New Zealand superannuation commences for` (Applicant OF Date 1 3 1960, FALSE, TRUE, 10, 40, 40, 15, FALSE, Date 1 1 1985, Date 15 4 2025, NOTHING) EQUALS Date 15 4 2025
-- the s 8 example: residence met on 1 July 2036, application 1 January 2036 (added after the independent pass)
#ASSERT `the day New Zealand superannuation commences for` (Applicant OF Date 30 6 1967, FALSE, TRUE, 14, 12, 14, 14, FALSE, Date 1 7 2022, Date 1 1 2036, JUST (Date 1 7 2036)) EQUALS Date 1 7 2036

-- s 4A
#ASSERT `is living alone` (Household OF TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is living alone` (Household OF TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is living alone` (Household OF FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Schedule 1, ss 17-19
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the single living alone rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `single` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the single sharing accommodation rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `couple` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the couple rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `couple` TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the single living alone rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 13 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the single living alone rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 14 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the hospital rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 20 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the single living alone rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `couple` FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the couple rate`
#ASSERT `the rate category for` (`rate facts` `couple` FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the hospital rate`
#ASSERT `the rate for` `the couple rate` `, rates` `the rates` EQUALS 760
#ASSERT `the rate for` `the hospital rate` `, rates` `the rates` EQUALS 300

§§ `Goal 2 — absence and payment overseas`

#ASSERT `is payable during the temporary absence` (`absent week` 20 `of` 28 `, unforeseeable:` FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is payable during the temporary absence` (`absent week` 27 `of` 28 `, unforeseeable:` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is payable during the temporary absence` (`absent week` 26 `of` 30 `, unforeseeable:` FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is payable during the temporary absence` (`absent week` 20 `of` 35 `, unforeseeable:` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is payable during the temporary absence` (`absent week` 20 `of` 35 `, unforeseeable:` TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` 104 `weeks, for medical treatment:` TRUE `, for aid work:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` 105 `weeks, for medical treatment:` TRUE `, for aid work:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` 156 `weeks, for medical treatment:` FALSE `, for aid work:` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` 157 `weeks, for medical treatment:` FALSE `, for aid work:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the chief executive may pay during an absence of` 50 `weeks, for medical treatment:` FALSE `, for aid work:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- s 26A: 270 months and 45 days: 270 + 1 = 271, over 540
#ASSERT `the proportion payable overseas for` (`residence of` 270 `months` 45 `days, years` 0) EQUALS 271 DIVIDED BY 540
#ASSERT `the proportion payable overseas for` (`residence of` 270 `months` 29 `days, years` 0) EQUALS 270 DIVIDED BY 540
#ASSERT `the proportion payable overseas for` (`residence of` 540 `months` 0 `days, years` 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the proportion payable overseas for` (`residence of` 600 `months` 0 `days, years` 0) EQUALS 1

-- s 32: base rate 900
#ASSERT `the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 25) `, base rate` 900 EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 20) `, base rate` 900 EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 15) `, base rate` 900 EQUALS 675
#ASSERT `the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 10) `, base rate` 900 EQUALS 450
-- s 32 gives no rate under 10 years (changed after the independent pass)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 9) `, base rate` 900)
#ASSERT `the Pacific rate for` (`residence of` 0 `months` 0 `days, years` 19.9) `, base rate` 900 EQUALS 855
#ASSERT `the last day overseas payments may run to, died` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS Date 29 3 2025

§§ `Goal 3 — the rates and the Fund`

#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 700 `, living alone` 455 `, sharing` 420 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 650 `, living alone` 422.5 `, sharing` 390 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 730 `, living alone` 474.5 `, sharing` 438 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 660 `, living alone` 429 `, sharing` 396 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 725 `, living alone` 471.25 `, sharing` 435 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the rates meet s 16, couple` 700 `, living alone` 450 `, sharing` 420 `, net average wage` 1000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the required annual capital contribution, percentage` 1.5 `, GDP` 400000 `, net cost` 5000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the required annual capital contribution, percentage` 0.5 `, GDP` 400000 `, net cost` 3000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 1000
#ASSERT `the most that may be withdrawn from the Fund, required contribution` (0 MINUS 1000) `, financial year starting` (Date 1 7 2020) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the most that may be withdrawn from the Fund, required contribution` (0 MINUS 1000) `, financial year starting` (Date 1 7 2019) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most that may be withdrawn from the Fund, required contribution` 1000 `, financial year starting` (Date 1 7 2024) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the Minister must explain a lesser contribution, required` 1000 `, to be paid` 500 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must explain a lesser contribution, required` (0 MINUS 10) `, to be paid` 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Minister must explain a lesser contribution, required` 1000 `, to be paid` 1000 EQUALS FALSE
-- Changed 2026-10-17 (Legislation Act s 55, applied at the user's direction): the deadline falls on a non-working day, so it runs to 3/7/2028.
#ASSERT `the latest the next performance review may be, last review` (Date 1 7 2023) EQUALS Date 3 7 2028

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 6 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `entitled` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 6 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `commences on` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 6 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `weekly rate before tax` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 6 2025, `rate facts` `couple` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `weekly rate before tax` EQUALS 760
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 1 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `entitled` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 1 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `weekly rate before tax` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the superannuation position for` (`Superannuation case` OF `a long resident`, Date 1 1 2025, `rate facts` `single` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE, `the rates`))'s `commences on` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (added 2026-10-17)`

-- 5 years after a review on 30 June 2023 end on Friday 30 June 2028: unchanged.
#ASSERT `the latest the next performance review may be, last review` (Date 30 6 2023) EQUALS Date 30 6 2028
